11
00:56:45,600 --> 00:56:51,600
Knocked Up is a 2007 American romantic comedy film written, produced and directed by Judd Apatow, and starring Seth
Rogen, Katherine Heigl, Paul Rudd, Leslie Mann, Jay Baruchel, Jonah Hill, Jason Segel and Martin Starr.

12
01:01:55,200 --> 01:02:01,200
It follows the repercussions of a drunken one-night stand between a slacker and a
recently promoted media personality that results in an unintended pregnancy.

13
01:07:04,800 --> 01:07:10,800
Knocked Up was directed by Apatow, from a screenplay by himself.

14
01:12:14,400 --> 01:12:20,400
Apatow, Shauna Robertson and Clayton Townsend were involved in the film
as producers for the film studio, Apatow Productions.

15
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:30,000
Rogen and Evan Goldberg were involved in the film as executive producers.

16
01:22:33,600 --> 01:22:39,600
Filming began in May 2006, in various locations in the United States, with a
focus on California, including Los Angeles and Santa Monica.

17
01:27:43,200 --> 01:27:49,200
The cinematography was in charge of Eric Edwards, while the soundtrack
was composed by Loudon Wainwright III and Joe Henry.

18
01:32:52,800 --> 01:32:58,800
The film was edited by Brent White and Craig Alpert.

19
01:38:02,400 --> 01:38:08,400
The film had a budget of $25 million.

20
01:43:12,000 --> 01:43:18,000
Knocked Up premiered at South by Southwest on March 12, 2007, and was released
in the United States on June 1, 2007, by Universal Pictures.

21
01:48:21,600 --> 01:48:27,600
The film was a box office success, grossing $219 million
worldwide, and received positive reviews from critics.

22
01:53:31,200 --> 01:53:37,200
This Is 40, a "sort-of sequel" focused on Rudd's and Mann's characters with Apatow
returning as writer/director, was released on December 21, 2012.

23
01:58:40,800 --> 01:58:46,800
The film explores themes of alcohol, pregnancy, bed, one-night stand, condom.

24
02:03:50,400 --> 02:03:56,400
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
